      "problem": "Compute $\\text{E}[-5X]$ if $\\text{E}[X]=-1.$",
      "worked_solution": "For any constant $a$ and any random variable $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX]=a\\text{E}[X].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[-5X] & =-5\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & =(-5)(-1) \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
